f":"#/$defs/ColorValue"},"onSuccess":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ColorValue"},"warning":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ColorValue"},"onWarning":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ColorValue"},"info":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ColorValue"},"onInfo":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ColorValue"},"stateLayer":{"type":"object","properties":{"hover":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1},"focus":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1},"pressed":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1},"disabled":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1}},"additionalProperties":false}},"additionalProperties":false},"ColorValue":{"type":"string","pattern":"^(#([0-9A-Fa-f]{6}|[0-9A-Fa-f]{8})|rgba?\\([^)]+\\)|\\{\\{[^}]+\\}\\})$"},"Component":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"DefinitionSource":{"anyOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\{\\{.*\\}\\}$","description":"Binding to a definition held in state (since v1.4)."},{"type":"string","description":"Resource URI on the current origin, e.g. `ui://pages/main`."},{"type":"object","description":"Qualified reference to a definition on another origin (since v1.4).","properties":{"$ref":{"type":"string","description":"Resource URI to read from the named origin."},"from":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Origin"}},"required":["$ref"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","description":"Inline PageDefinition or WidgetDefinition."}],"description":"Where a definition comes from. Four forms: an inline definition, a resource\nURI on the current origin, a qualified `{ $ref, from }` reference to another\norigin, or a binding to a definition already held in state.\n\nOmitting `from` means the current origin, so every pre-1.4 document keeps its\nexact meaning. Naming an origin makes that origin ambient for the resolved\nsubtree — its tool calls, resource reads, state, storage and permissions all\nscope to it. See `01_Core_Concepts.md` §1.9 and `07_Security.md` §7.10.\n\nAccepted wherever `RouteValue` is accepted (§1.2.1) and as the `source` of the\n`view` widget (§2.13.1)."},"Density":{"type":"object","properties":{"comfortable":{"$ref":"#/$defs/DensityValue"},"standard":{"$ref":"#/$defs/DensityValue"},"compact":{"$ref":"#/$defs/DensityValue"},"active":{"enum":["comfortable","standard","compact"]}},"additionalProperties":false},"DensityValue":{"type":"object","properties":{"vertical":{"type":"number","minimum":-4,"maximum":4},"horizontal":{"type":"number","minimum":-4,"maximum":4}},"required":["vertical","horizontal"],"additionalProperties":false},"Dimension":{"oneOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"oneOf":[{"type":"number"},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}]},"unit":{"type":"string"}},"required":["value"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}],"description":"Numeric size — accepts a plain `number` (logical pixels) OR the\nlegacy MCP UI DSL v1.0 `{value, unit}` object form. The `unit`\nfield is informational; the runtime treats every dimension as\nlogical pixels. `value` may itself be a binding: a bar whose width\ncomes from data writes `{\"value\": \"{{item.ratio}}\", \"unit\": \"percent\"}`,\nand that is the whole point of the object form."},"EdgeInsets":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"object","properties":{"value":{"type":"number"},"unit":{"type":"string"}},"required":["value"]},{"type":"object","properties":{"all":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"horizontal":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"vertical":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"top":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"right":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"bottom":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"left":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"}}},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}],"description":"Space around or inside a box. Four spellings, all accepted wherever insets\nare expected:\n\n- **Number** — one value applied to every edge.\n- **`{value, unit}`** — the legacy v1.0 dimension object; `unit` is\n  informational and the runtime treats every inset as logical pixels.\n- **Edge map** — `{all}` for every edge, `{horizontal, vertical}` for the\n  two axes, or `{top, right, bottom, left}` for individual edges. Each entry\n  is a `Dimension`, so one edge may be bound while its neighbours are\n  literal: `{ \"left\": \"{{sidebar.width}}\", \"top\": 8 }`.\n- **Binding** — resolves to any of the above at render time.\n\nA bare word is not an inset: the runtime resolves it to null and the widget\nfalls back to no padding, so validators reject it rather than let it render\nas a silent zero."},"Elevation":{"type":"object","properties":{"level0":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ElevationLevel"},"level1":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ElevationLevel"},"level2":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ElevationLevel"},"level3":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ElevationLevel"},"level4":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ElevationLevel"},"level5":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ElevationLevel"}},"additionalProperties":false},"ElevationLevel":{"oneOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"object","properties":{"shadow":{"type":"number"},"tint":{"type":"number"}},"additionalProperties":false}]},"FocusRing":{"type":"object","properties":{"color":{"$ref":"#/$defs/ColorValue"},"width":{"type":"number"},"offset":{"type":"number"},"radius":{"type":"number"}},"additionalProperties":false},"FontRegistry":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"type":"object","properties":{"weights":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"$ref":"#/$defs/AssetRef"}},"variableAxes":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"tag":{"type":"string","minLength":4,"maxLength":4},"min":{"type":"number"},"max":{"type":"number"},"default":{"type":"number"}},"required":["tag","min","max"],"additionalProperties":false}},"fallbacks":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"additionalProperties":false},"description":"Font asset registration. Map of font family name → asset\ndeclaration. Each declaration tells the runtime which file to\nload for a given weight/style and, for variable fonts, which\naxes are tunable.\n\n- `weights` — map of weight value (`100`..`900` or `regular`/\n  `bold`/etc.) to AssetRef. Set per file you want to ship.\n- `variableAxes` — list of variable-font axis tunings. Each entry\n  is `{tag, min, max, default}`. Standard axes: `wght` (weight),\n  `wdth` (width), `opsz` (optical size), `ital` (italic), `slnt`\n  (slant). Custom axes (`GRAD`, `XOPQ`, etc.) are accepted by tag.\n  When set, `weights` becomes optional — the runtime drives the\n  `wght` axis from text.style.fontWeight.\n- `fallbacks` — ordered family-name list used when a glyph isn't\n  in the primary font (CJK, emoji, math)."},"Gradient":{"type":"object","properties":{"type":{"enum":["linear","radial","sweep"]},"colors":{"type":"array","items":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Color"},"minItems":2},"stops":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1}},"begin":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Alignment"},"end":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Alignment"},"center":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Alignment"},"radius":{"type":"number","minimum":0},"startAngle":{"type":"number"},"endAngle":{"type":"number"},"tileMode":{"enum":["clamp","repeated","mirror"],"default":"clamp"}},"required":["type","colors"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Multi-stop gradient fill. Selected by `type`:\n\n- `linear` — straight axis from `begin` (default `centerLeft`) to\n  `end` (default `centerRight`).\n- `radial` — circular gradient out from `center` (default `center`)\n  to `radius` (default `0.5`, expressed as a fraction of the\n  bounding rectangle's longest side).\n- `sweep` — angular gradient around `center`, swept from\n  `startAngle` (default `0`) to `endAngle` (default `2π`) in\n  radians.\n\n`colors` lists at least two color values; `stops` (optional) places\neach color at a position in `[0, 1]`. `tileMode` controls behaviour\npast the gradient extents."},"IconRef":{"$comment":"anyOf, not oneOf: the name branch is an unconstrained string, so a binding expression matches both it and the Binding branch. `oneOf` reads that legitimate value as a violation — the same reason the Widget union uses anyOf.","anyOf":[{"type":"string","description":"Icon name, or an AssetRef string (scheme-prefixed, or an `assets/` path)."},{"type":"object","properties":{"codepoint":{"type":"integer"},"fontFamily":{"type":"string"},"fontPackage":{"type":"string"}},"required":["codepoint"],"additionalProperties":false},{"type":"object","properties":{"uri":{"type":"string","description":"Resource uri read through MCP `resources/read` on the resolved origin."},"origin":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Origin"}},"required":["uri"],"additionalProperties":false},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}],"description":"Reference to an icon. Three forms, all accepted anywhere an icon is\ntaken — the `icon` widget and every widget with an icon slot\n(`button.icon`, `iconButton.icon`, `floatingActionButton.icon`,\n`popupMenuButton.icon`, `rating.icon`, `offlineFallback.icon`,\n`permissionPrompt.icon`, …):\n\n1. **Name** — `\"home\"`, `\"folder_open\"`, … resolved through the\n   runtime's built-in icon table. Zero-cost, and the default reading of\n   a bare string.\n2. **Codepoint** — `{codepoint, fontFamily?, fontPackage?}` for glyphs\n   the name table does not carry.\n3. **`AssetRef`** — any form that primitive accepts (network URL,\n   `bundle://`, `assets/`, `data:image/svg+xml;…`, `client://`, or the\n   `{uri, origin?}` object). Which of those a runtime resolves is\n   declared, not assumed (`06_Runtime_Contract.md` §6.12).\n\nA bare string carrying a known scheme prefix (or an `assets/` path) is\nan asset; every other bare string is a **name**. That rule is what lets\nthe named form stay the zero-ceremony default while the same slot also\naccepts a server-served glyph.\n\nThis primitive exists so the rule is stated once. Before it, `icon`\ndocumented three forms while the eight other icon slots were typed as\nbare strings — so the same value was legal in one slot and undeclared\nin the next, and a codepoint object could not be written at all outside\nthe `icon` widget."},"Motion":{"type":"object","properties":{"duration":{"type":"object","properties":{"short1":{"type":"number"},"short2":{"type":"number"},"short3":{"type":"number"},"short4":{"type":"number"},"medium1":{"type":"number"},"medium2":{"type":"number"},"medium3":{"type":"number"},"medium4":{"type":"number"},"long1":{"type":"number"},"long2":{"type":"number"},"long3":{"type":"number"},"long4":{"type":"number"},"extraLong":{"type":"number"}},"additionalProperties":{"type":"number"}},"easing":{"type":"object","properties":{"standard":{"type":"string"},"emphasized":{"type":"string"},"decelerate":{"type":"string"},"accelerate":{"type":"string"}},"additionalProperties":{"type":"string"}}},"additionalProperties":false},"NavigationStyle":{"type":"object","properties":{"backgroundColor":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Color"},"backgroundImage":{"$ref":"#/$defs/BackgroundImage"},"indicatorColor":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Color","description":"Selection indicator pill color (rail / drawer / tabs)."},"indicatorShape":{"$ref":"#/$defs/BorderRadius","description":"Selection indicator corner radius. Defaults to a fully-rounded pill."},"dividerColor":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Color","description":"Drawer-only — color of dividers between item groups."},"dividerThickness":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"dividerIndent":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension","description":"Drawer-only — leading inset before each divider."},"labelStyle":{"$ref":"#/$defs/TextStyle","description":"Default text style for item labels (selected and unselected). Per-item override via NavItem.style.labelStyle."},"iconStyle":{"type":"object","properties":{"color":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Color"},"size":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Default icon color and size."},"selectedColor":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Color","description":"Foreground color (icon + label) for the selected item."},"unselectedColor":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Color","description":"Foreground color for non-selected items."},"elevation":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Visual styling for a navigation surface (drawer / rail / tabs /\nbottomBar). Every field is optional — omitted fields fall back to\nthe active theme's component defaults. Used by\n`NavigationConfig.style` (whole surface) and `NavItem.style`\n(per-item override).\n\nBackgrounds compose: `backgroundColor` paints first, then\n`backgroundImage` paints over it."},"Opacity":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":{"type":"number","minimum":0,"maximum":1}},"Origin":{"type":"object","properties":{"connection":{"oneOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\{\\{.*\\}\\}$"}],"description":"Outbound MCP client connection id, or a binding to one."}},"required":["connection"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Who serves a definition. Deliberately open so future sources need no new\nsyntax — today one shape is defined; `{ \"bundle\": ... }` / `{ \"agent\": ... }`\nand similar can be added without changing any document that uses it.\n\n`connection` names a live connection in the host's outbound MCP client\nregistry, addressed by the id used to open it. The DSL does not define how\nconnections are made — that is a host capability (`06_Runtime_Contract.md`\n§6.11.1); it defines only how a definition is addressed once one exists.\n\nA binding is the normal value here: an application opens its connections in\n`lifecycle.onInit` and keeps the ids in state.\n\nRuntimes MUST reject an Origin whose sole key they do not recognise rather\nthan falling back to the current origin — a permissive reading would render a\ndifferent server's UI under the requested one's identity (`07_Security.md`\n§7.10.1)."},"RouteTransition":{"type":"object","properties":{"style":{"enum":["slide","fade","scale","cube","sharedAxis","fadeThrough"]},"duration":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension","description":"Total transition duration in milliseconds. Defaults to the M3 motion-system value for the chosen style."},"curve":{"$ref":"#/$defs/AnimationCurve","description":"Easing curve for the transition's progress. Defaults to `emphasized`."},"axis":{"enum":["horizontal","vertical"],"description":"Direction for `slide` / `sharedAxis`. Defaults to `horizontal`."},"reverse":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"When true, run the transition in reverse direction (for back navigation)."}},"required":["style"],"additionalProperties":false,"description":"Per-route page transition. Declared on a `RouteValue` so every\n`navigate` to that route uses the same transition, OR overridden\ninline on a `navigate` action. Six canonical styles:\n\n- `slide` — incoming page slides over the outgoing along the\n  direction (M3 default for forward navigation).\n- `fade` — cross-fade between pages at the same position.\n- `scale` — outgoing scales out, incoming scales in.\n- `cube` — perspective-rotate as if turning a 3D cube; needs a\n  perspective-aware compositor (falls back to `slide` when\n  unavailable).\n- `sharedAxis` — coordinated slide+fade across an axis (M3 motion\n  pattern for sibling-level navigation).\n- `fadeThrough` — outgoing fades out while incoming fades in\n  after a brief zero-opacity bridge (M3 motion pattern for\n  top-level navigation)."},"Shape":{"type":"object","properties":{"none":{"$ref":"#/$defs/BorderRadius"},"extraSmall":{"$ref":"#/$defs/BorderRadius"},"small":{"$ref":"#/$defs/BorderRadius"},"medium":{"$ref":"#/$defs/BorderRadius"},"large":{"$ref":"#/$defs/BorderRadius"},"extraLarge":{"$ref":"#/$defs/BorderRadius"},"full":{"$ref":"#/$defs/BorderRadius"}},"additionalProperties":{"$ref":"#/$defs/BorderRadius"}},"Spacing":{"type":"object","properties":{"xxs":{"type":"number"},"xs":{"type":"number"},"sm":{"type":"number"},"md":{"type":"number"},"lg":{"type":"number"},"xl":{"type":"number"},"2xl":{"type":"number"},"3xl":{"type":"number"},"4xl":{"type":"number"},"screenPadding":{"type":"number"},"cardPadding":{"type":"number"},"sectionGap":{"type":"number"},"inlineGap":{"type":"number"}},"additionalProperties":{"type":"number"}},"TextStyle":{"oneOf":[{"type":"string","pattern":"^\\{\\{.*\\}\\}$","description":"Binding expression that resolves to a TextStyle object — typically `{{theme.typography.<role>}}`."},{"type":"object","properties":{"fontFamily":{"oneOf":[{"type":"string"},{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}]},"fontSize":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"fontWeight":{"anyOf":[{"type":"number"},{"type":"string","pattern":"^[1-9]00$","description":"CSS numeric spelling (`\"700\"`). Documents written against CSS habits use it, and the runtime reads it the same as the number."},{"enum":["thin","extraLight","light","normal","medium","semiBold","bold","extraBold","black","regular","w100","w200","w300","w400","w500","w600","w700","w800","w900"]},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}]},"fontStyle":{"oneOf":[{"enum":["normal","italic"]},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}]},"color":{"type":"string"},"backgroundColor":{"type":"string"},"letterSpacing":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"wordSpacing":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"height":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension","description":"Line-height multiplier — `height * fontSize` is the per-line vertical advance."},"decoration":{"oneOf":[{"enum":["none","underline","overline","lineThrough"]},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}]},"decorationColor":{"type":"string"},"decorationStyle":{"oneOf":[{"enum":["solid","double","dotted","dashed","wavy"]},{"$ref":"#/$defs/Binding"}]},"decorationThickness":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"},"fontFeatures":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"OpenType feature tags (`smcp`, `lnum`, `tnum`, `liga`, `dlig`, …)."},"shadows":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"color":{"type":"string"},"offset":{"type":"object","properties":{"dx":{"type":"number"},"dy":{"type":"number"},"x":{"type":"number"},"y":{"type":"number"}},"additionalProperties":false,"description":"`{dx, dy}` (canonical) or `{x, y}` (legacy alias) offset."},"blurRadius":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Dimension"}},"required":["color"],"additionalProperties":false}},"shader":{"$ref":"#/$defs/Gradient","description":"Gradient/shader fill applied to the rendered text via a shader mask. When set, `color` is ignored."}},"additionalProperties":true}],"description":"Inline text style applied per `text` widget instance. Layered on\ntop of an M3 typography role when `variant` is set, or used\nstandalone. Mirrors the theme `TextStyle` token shape (fontFamily,\nfontSize, fontWeight, lineHeight, letterSpacing, fontFeatureSettings)\nand adds the per-instance fields a content app needs: color,\ndecoration, shader (gradient fill), and shadow stack.\n\nThe object stays open. Documents in the field carry keys this style\nnever had — `textAlign` inside `style` is the common one, written by\nhand before it moved onto the widget — and the runtime simply ignores\nthem. Rejecting them here would not correct anything: validation runs\nwhen the document loads, so a stray key inside `style` would stop the\nwhole page instead of being ignored the way the runtime ignores it."},"ThemePreset":{"enum":["warm","cool","sepia","mono","highContrast"],"description":"Curated content-app theme bundle. Five named presets cover the\ncommon content-app moods. When set, the preset is applied first\n(color scheme + typography + spacing tone) and individual theme\nfields then layer overrides on top — so authors can pick a preset\nand tweak just one or two fields rather than building the whole\ntheme from scratch.\n\nPresets (color tone · typography character · spacing density):\n- `warm` — book-shelf paper tones, serif typography, cozy spacing.\n- `cool` — album / streaming ambient. Cool blues, sans-serif,\n  standard spacing.\n- `sepia` — long-form reading. Aged-paper background, increased\n  line-height, narrower content column.\n- `mono` — typography-led, neutral grays, generous line-height,\n  minimal accents.\n- `highContrast` — accessibility-first. WCAG AAA contrast ratios,\n  enlarged hit targets, bold weights."},"Typography":{"type":"object","properties":{"displayLarge":{"$ref":"#/$defs/TextStyle"},"displayMedium":{"$ref":"#/$defs/TextStyle"},"displaySmall":{"$ref":"#/$defs/TextStyle"},"headlineLarge":{"$ref":"